# ovh_dedicated_server_networking

Manage the network interfaces aggregation (bonding) of a dedicated server.

~> **WARNING** Changing the aggregation reinstalls the server networking and is a `ForceNew` operation. A public interface can only be aggregated with another public interface, and a vrack interface with another vrack interface: you cannot bond three interfaces and leave one alone, nor separate all four.

## Example Usage

{{tffile "examples/resources/dedicated_server_networking/example_1.tf"}}

## Argument Reference

The following arguments are supported:

* `service_name` - (Required) The internal name of your dedicated server.
* `interfaces` - (Required) One or two interface aggregation blocks describing how the server NICs are grouped. Each block supports:
  * `macs` - (Required) The list of MAC addresses of the physical interfaces to aggregate.
  * `type` - (Required) The network type of the interface (`public` or `vrack`).

## Attributes Reference

The following attributes are exported:

* `description` - Operation description.
* `status` - Operation status.
* `interfaces` - In addition to the arguments above, each interface block exports:
  * `aggregation_fallback` - MAC address of the LACP fallback interface (the address the aggregation falls back to when the bond degrades to a single link).
